## Overview

The TOOLCHAIN module provisions a pinned Rust toolchain for a target
triple and compiles staged source into portable OxDock binaries, all
under a dedicated `toolchain` cache group. `TOOLCHAIN_ENSURE` lays out
the cache and returns the cached `cargo`, `rustc`, and sysroot paths.
`TOOLCHAIN_FETCH_SOURCE` snapshots local source into the cache (v1
bundle; pinned remote fetch is follow-up). `TOOLCHAIN_BUILD`
compiles with the cached toolchain only, provisioning automatically
when the binaries are missing and rebuilding only when the
fingerprint (source plus features plus profile plus linker plus
toolchain versions) goes stale. Linking rides a cached zig linker
provisioned beside the toolchain (Apple targets on macOS hosts use
the host compiler for its SDK explicitly), the cached `rustc` rides
`RUSTC`, and registries live in a cache-scoped `CARGO_HOME`, so no
host compiler, toolchain, or registry leaks in. Release is the
default profile; `dev` is an explicit opt-in whose outputs never read
releasable. Import it with `IMPORT [STD, TOOLCHAIN]` in a runner
built with the `toolchain` feature. The function reference below
lists every entry with signatures.

Snapshot a demo package into the cache. This runs end to end with no
network: the staged copy is content addressed under the toolchain
group.

```oxdock
IMPORT [STD, TOOLCHAIN]

# Stage a demo package with a manifest and one source file.
MKDIR demo-src
WRITE demo-src/Cargo.toml '[package]\nname = "demo-pkg"\nversion = "0.1.0"\n'
MKDIR demo-src/src
WRITE demo-src/src/main.rs 'fn main() {}\n'

# Snapshot the package into the cache; the staged copy is content addressed.
LET $s: MAP = TOOLCHAIN_FETCH_SOURCE("demo-src")
ASSERT_CONTAINS $s.manifest_dir "local-"
```

Build argument shapes fail before any provisioning or network use.
An unknown profile never reaches the toolchain.

```oxdock expect_error:"profile must be"
IMPORT [STD, TOOLCHAIN]

# Stage the same demo package first.
MKDIR demo-src
WRITE demo-src/Cargo.toml '[package]\nname = "demo-pkg"\nversion = "0.1.0"\n'
LET $s: MAP = TOOLCHAIN_FETCH_SOURCE("demo-src")

# An unknown profile fails before any toolchain provisioning or network use.
LET $b: MAP = TOOLCHAIN_BUILD("", $s.manifest_dir, [], {profile: "bogus"})
```

Unknown architectures fail closed instead of guessing a toolchain.

```oxdock expect_error:"unknown target triple"
IMPORT [STD, TOOLCHAIN]

# No triple is ever guessed from an unknown name.
LET $t: MAP = TOOLCHAIN_ENSURE("mips-unknown-linux-gnu")
```
